      "explanation": "The doctor never actively asked about fever, dysuria, hematuria, chest tightness, palpitations, or other action-blocking symptoms. The patient did not report any spontaneously, and the doctor relied on the established contact plan without performing the mandatory targeted screening for infection or cardiopulmonary symptoms. This omission constitutes a minor responsibility-chain error.",
